QuestGuidance.Register("en",197,{
[6273]="7003707B\n1\tBring the note to Dudsig\tYou should bring the note you found to Dudsig.\n2\tBring the note you found to Dudsig in Oserley\tDudsig is near the stable in Oserley, east of the brigands' camp. You should bring the note you found to Dudsig.\n",
[6274]="70057188\n1\tClimb atop the Carrock\tThe Carrock can be found in the Beorninglands. You should climb to the top of the Carrock and meet Léothred there.\n2\tLook out from atop the Carrock\tThe Carrock can be found in the Beorninglands. You should look out from the top of the Carrock.\n3\tTalk to Léothred atop the Carrock\tLéothred can be found at the Carrock. You should talk to Léothred.\n4\tComplete \"To the Floodfells\"\tLéothred can be found at Limlók in the Floodfells. You should travel to Limlók.\n5\tTalk to Léothred at Limlók\tLéothred can be found at Limlók in the Floodfells. You should travel to Limlók.\n",
[6275]="700551E5\n1\tCollect stone-rubbings from the tombs of Aufaltor\tTombs can be found throughout Aufaltor in Thuringwath.\n2\tCollect stone-rubbings from the tombs of Aufaltor (total: 10)\tTombs can be found throughout Aufaltor in Thuringwath. Fading inscriptions on the ancient tombs of Aufaltor might be preserved through stone-rubbings. You should take stone-rubbings of the tombs of Aufaltor.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have collected many stone-rubbings from the tombs at Aufaltor.\n",
[6276]="7001752B\n1\tDefeat Uammaethor\030Defeat Nestaduan\030Defeat Grog\030Defeat Grothulun\030Defeat Ulugon\tSkûmfil lies to the south-east of the Shadowed Refuge. Moggi sent you to Skûmfil to destroy the warrior-gredbyg there who have some manner of independence from the queen Brúmbereth. The chief of these is Uammaethor.\n2\tTalk to Moggi at the Shadowed Refuge\tMoggi is at the Shadowed Refuge, north-west of Skûmfil. You found and kill the grodbog-warrior Uammaethor and its defenders within the corpse-ridden place called Skûmfil.\n",
[6277]="70050212\n1\tDefeat Hládek the Hoary, Scourge of Thikil-gundu\tHládek the Hoary poses a grave threat to all that seek the knowledge buried within Thikil-gundu.\n2\tDefeat Hládek the Hoary, Scourge of Thikil-gundu\tHládek the Hoary poses a grave threat to all that seek the knowledge buried within Thikil-gundu.\n3\tCompleted\tHládek the Hoary poses a grave threat to all that seek the knowledge buried within Thikil-gundu.\n",
[6278]="7004A818\n1\tGather supplies in Dâr Mauzur (total: 10)\tBregdal has asked you to gather any supplies you might find in Dâr Mauzur.\n2\tBring the supplies to Bregdal\tBregdal can be found on the border of Talath Úrui and Dor Amarth. You should bring the supplies to Bregdal.\n",
[6279]="700088F7\n1\tDeliver the food-sacks to Emissary Pip Diggins at Ost Ringdyr\030Collect food-sacks (total: 5)\tThe goblin-village of Grothum lies far to the north-east of Hoarhallow. Emissary Pip Diggins asked you to recover food stolen from Hoarhallow. He directed you to search among the goblin village at Grothum or on the persons of the enemy.\n",
[6280]="7004A9D5\n1\tGather rations\tGather rations.\n2\tGather rations (total: 8)\tGather rations.\n3\tBring the rations to the hobbits' guest-hall, near Cormallen\tA collection box can be found in the hobbits' guest-hall, near Cormallen. Bring the rations to the hobbits' guest-hall.\n",
[6281]="7001670F\n1\tDefeat the Orc-emissary at Uruk-gashan\030Defeat the Orc-emissary at Drû-garmadh\030Defeat the Orc-emissary at Athmadhul\tMoria Orc-emissaries can be found at Uruk-gashan, Drû-garmadh, and Athmadhul. Raskwith asked to go to the three Orc-camps in the Dimrill Dale and defeat the three Moria Orc-emissaries.\n2\tTalk to Raskwith at Mekhem-bizru\tRaskwith is at Mekhem-bizru, north-west of the Orc-camps. Raskwith will be pleased to hear the Moria Orc-emissaries have been defeated.\n",
[6282]="70045101\n1\tTalk to Malhar\tTalk to Malhar when you are ready to begin the journey out of the Mouths of Entwash.\n2\tGo with Malhar\tAccompany Malhar on the path out of the Mouths of Entwash.\n3\tTalk to Malhar\tMalhar has stopped for a rest at a point in the Mouths of Entwash. Talk to him and see if you can be of any help.\n4\tFill the water-skin\030Find water\tFind fresh water near Malhar, at a point in the Mouths of Entwash, and fill his empty water-skin.\n5\tGive Malhar the water-skin\tBring the filled water-skin to Malhar, where he waits at a point in the Mouths of Entwash.\n6\tGo with Malhar\tAccompany Malhar on the path out of the Mouths of Entwash.\n7\tTalk to Malhar\tMalhar has stopped for a rest at a point in the Mouths of Entwash. Talk to him and see if you can be of any help.\n8\tScout ahead to the south\030Scout ahead to the west\030Scout ahead to the south-west\tMalhar has asked you to scout ahead, south and west of the point where he has stopped in the Mouths of Entwash.\n9\tReturn to Malhar\tReturn to Malhar where he waits at a point in the Mouths of Entwash and describe what you saw scouting ahead.\n10\tGo with Malhar\tAccompany Malhar on the path out of the Mouths of Entwash.\n11\tTalk to Malhar\tMalhar has stopped on his path in the Mouths of Entwash. Talk to him to hear what he has to say.\n12\tInvestigate the sounds\tInvestigate the noises Malhar thinks he heard, just south of the point he stopped in the Mouths of Entwash.\n13\tDefend yourself\tThe noises Malhar heard ahead of him in the Mouths of Entwash turned out to be a Variag ambush!\n14\tReturn to Malhar\tReturn to Malhar where he waits at a point in the Mouths of Entwash and let him know that the path ahead is clear.\n15\tGo with Malhar\tAccompany Malhar on the path out of the Mouths of Entwash.\n16\tTalk to Malhar\tMalhar stopped again, just as the Beacon Hills came into full view. Talk to him to hear what he has to say.\n17\tReturn to Glánhar\tYou have led Malhar safely out of the Mouths of Entwash. Go with him to Glánhar in the centre of Ost Rimmon.\n",
[6283]="7002F002\n1\t'Mount' the hobby-horse\tThe hobby-horse is near Harwick's Mead Hall. To run the race, you must first have a hobby-horse.\n2\t'Ride' through the first gate\tThe first gate is ahead. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\t'Ride' through the second gate\tReach the second gate. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\t'Ride' through the third gate\tRide through the third gate. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n5\t'Ride' through the fourth gate\tRide through the fourth gate. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n6\t'Ride' through the fifth gate\tRide through the fifth gate. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n7\t'Ride' through the sixth gate\tRide through the sixth gate. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n8\t'Ride' through the seventh gate\tRide through the seventh gate. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n9\t'Ride' through the eighth gate\tRide through the eighth gate. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n10\t'Ride' through the ninth gate\tRide through the ninth gate. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n11\t'Ride' through the tenth gate\tRide through the tenth gate. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n12\t'Ride' through the eleventh gate\tRide through the eleventh gate. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n13\t'Ride' through the twelfth gate\tRide through the twelfth gate. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n14\tReturn to Garbrand\tGarbrand is outside the Mead Hall of Harwick.\n",
[6284]="7000A295\n1\tCollect the hobgoblins' recipe\030Burn bubbling pots with torches (total: 3)\tThe goblin-camp is in the Bleakleaf Crest, south of Dwaling. Bob Greeneaves wants you to burn the pots the goblins are using to cook down the spiders, as well as recover the recipe for their tar.\n2\tBring the hobgoblins' recipe to Bob Greeneaves\tBob Greeneaves is in Dwaling, north of the Bleakleaf Crest. You should return to Bob Greeneaves with the news of your success.\n",
[6285]="7005AAF3\n1\tDefeat hobgoblins in Uzdarulzahar (total: 12)\tThe Battle of Uzdarulzahar is underway! You should defeat hobgoblins in Uzdarulzahar.\n2\tCompleted\tThe battle proceeds!\n",
[6286]="7003EF09\n1\tComplete to receive a map to the Hobnanigans Fields!\tHobnanigans is a treasured pastime of the hobbits from the Shire. They have brought the unique game to the festival grounds north of Bree. What could possibly go wrong when you give a dozen adventurers sticks and put a chicken in the middle?\n2\tComplete to receive a map to the Hobnanigans Fields!\tHobnanigans is a treasured pastime of the hobbits from the Shire. They have brought the unique game to the festival grounds north of Bree. What could possibly go wrong when you give a dozen adventurers sticks and put a chicken in the middle?\n",
[6287]="70037DB4\n1\tDefend the wall against the attacking waves ([see journal]/12)\tThe armies of Saruman are using siege weapons to fire hook and chain attachments onto the walls of the Hornburg. The ballista hooks are able to cause damage to the structure of the Rohirrim defences once they have latched on. The defences must disable the hooks and hold the defences for a moment longer, while Théoden King plans the counter-attack. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[6288]="70009EF7\n1\tDefeat Free Peoples in the Isendeep Mine (total: 10)\tFight off invaders who meant to take the Isendeep mine. You must fight the foe within the Isendeep mine and drive them out for the glory of Angmar.\n2\tTalk to Task-master Bárzqhosh\030Talk to War-tyrant Akúlhun\tIf the mine is fallen or Taskmaster Bárzqhosh is fallen in the battle, make your way to Gramsfoot and speak with War-tyrant Akúlhun. Your success is complete. Return to Taskmaster Bárzqhosh and tell him of your victory.\n",
[6289]="7002F9A1\n1\tSpeak to Acdreda east of Sahard's farmstead\tAcdreda defends the area directly east of Sahard's farmstead. Norbald has spotted a band of Uruk riders moving towards Acdreda's position.\n2\tDefeat Uruk-hai Raiders (total: 2)\030Defeat Uruk-hai Skirmishers (total: 2)\tThe Uruk-hai riders are east of Acdreda's position. Acdreda requires aid in defending the eastern farms from the enemy riders. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tSpeak to Acdreda east of Sahard's farm\tAcdreda defends outside the eastern edge of Sahard's farm. Acdreda awaits to hear of your confrontation with the Uruk-hai riders.\n4\tSpeak to Thane Elfmar at the Mead Hall of Faldham\tElfmar musters the other riders at the Mead Hall of Faldham. Acdreda hopes that Elfmar has rallied the remaining men for the main assault against Faldham.\n",
[6290]="70046B1D\n1\tDefeat enemies in Osgiliath (total: 10)\tDefeat enemies hiding in Osgiliath.\n2\tTalk to Mablung\tYou should talk to Mablung, who can be found at the Ranger encampment in after-battle Osgiliath.\n",
[6291]="70015E46\n1\tBring the holly-leaves to Celebrandir in Gwingris\030Collect holly-leaves (total: 8)\tHolly-trees can be found throughout Glâd Ereg. Celebrandir is encamped at Gwingris in the northern reaches of Glâd Ereg. You should gather more holly-leaves and bring them to the Elf Celebrandir.\n",
[6292]="70040A00\n1\tRefugees from Lothgobel can be found around Calembel. You should tell the refugees that it is safe for them to return, for the Corsairs have pulled out.\t\n2\tReturn to Laindir\tLaindir is in Calembel. You should return to Laindir to tell him the refugees have been informed of the good news.\n",
[6293]="70067163\n1\tFind Bezab's lost helmet somewhere in the water channel that runs through Furukzahar\tBezab dropped his favourite helmet over the railing in Furukzahar and it fell into the water channel that runs through the fortress.\n2\tExamine Bezab's lost helmet in the cave-claw nest by the water channel that runs through Furukzahar\tYou found Bezab's lost helmet beside the water channel that runs through Furukzahar, but it seems a cave-claw found it first.\n3\tTalk to Bezab south of the entrance to the throne in Furukzahar\tBezab is south of the entrance to the throne in Furukzahar, waiting to hear if you found his lost helmet.\n",
[6294]="7006B5FC\n1\tTalk to Turizi\tTurizi has been troubled since returning home from the war in the north. You should talk to him behind the house at Ekagar.\n",
[6295]="70044E3F\n1\tTalk to Lili Gardhur, the healer in Maur Tulhau\tBingo has eaten too much at the Welcoming Feast, and has asked you to find a healer in Maur Tulhau who might have a remedy for him.\n2\tTea plants can be found outside Maur Tulhau, in the Gloomglens. Lili Gardhur gave you a knife and sent you to look for suitable tea plants outside Maur Tulhau.\t\n3\tBring the tea flushes to Lili Gardhur in Maur Tulhau\tLili Gardhur is in the central square of Maur Tulhau, in the Gloomglens.\n4\tBring the medicinal tea to Bingo in the north-east corner of Maur Tulhau\tBingo is in the north-east corner of Maur Tulhau, suffering from an unhappy stomach. Lili Gardhur gave you some medicinal tea to bring to Bingo.\n5\tTalk to Theodore Gorse in Maur Tulhau\030Talk to Haley Meadowsweet in Maur Tulhau\030Talk to Iola Isbrun in Maur Tulhau\tBingo and his companions are in the north-east corner of Maur Tulhau.\n6\tTalk to Bingo in Maur Tulhau\tBingo has finished the medicinal tea, and now you should see if he is feeling better.\n7\tTalk to Lili Gardhur in Maur Tulhau\tLili Gardhur is in the central square of Maur Tulhau. Lili's medicinal tea did not seem to help Bingo's condition, and he asked you to see if she had any other remedies that might work instead.\n8\tPick up hot tea from the milestone in Maur Tulhau\tA hot pot of tea is brewing on the milestone in the centre of Maur Tulhau. Lili Gardhur thinks that the other tea you brought to Bingo might have cooled too much to be effective, and she wants you to bring him another pot of tea with more haste.\n9\tTalk to Bingo in Maur Tulhau\tBingo is in the north-east corner of Maur Tulhau, sipping the tea you brought to him.\n10\tTalk to Iola Isbrun in Maur Tulhau\tIola Isbrun is in the north-east corner of Maur Tulhau.\n11\tTalk to Bingo in Maur Tulhau\tBingo is in the north-east corner of Maur Tulhau.\n",
[6296]="7002824D\n1\tAid Mabon in searching the homestead\tMabon is just east of the homestead in the northern Starkmoor. Mabon needs your help to drive the raiders out of his father's homestead and protect the valuables within.\n2\tTalk to Mabon at Andras' homestead\tMabon is just east of the Homestead in the northern Starkmoor. Mabon will want to speak with you about the raid.\n",
[6297]="7000C3D0\n1\tTalk to Nan Henwood\030Talk to Rúni\030Talk to Barchiril\030Talk to Andy Brockhouse\tSpeak with one of the housing brokers that can be found in Eriador. These housing brokers can be found: - Across the river from Duillond - Across the river, west of Thorin's Gate - South of Michel Delving - South-east of Staddle\n",
[6298]="70046C4F\n1\tVisit the Cape of Belfalas\tYou can take the horse by the housing broker in either Dol Amroth, Pelargir, or Minas Tirith. You should visit and take a tour of the Cape of Belfalas housing and environs.\n2\tTalk to Falastír\tFalastír is located at the lighthouse on the Cape of Belfalas. The housing broker has recommended that you speak with Falastír, the old lighthouse keeper.\n",
[6299]="7005624D\n1\tVisit the Rohan Kingstead Neighbourhoods\030Visit the Rohan Eastfold Homesteads\030Visit the Kingstead Neighbourhood's town centre\030Visit the Eastfold Homestead's town centre\030Visit one of the houses in the Kingstead neighbourhood\030Visit one of the houses in the Eastfold Homesteads\030Visit one of the mead halls in the Kingstead neighbourhoods\030Visit one of the mead halls in the Eastfold Homesteads\tThe Kingstead and Eastfold Homesteads can be found in Rohan. You should visit and explore the Kingstead and Eastfold Homesteads.\n2\tTalk to Burginda\030Talk to Seleflad\tBurginda can be found at Edoras or the Kingstead neighbourhoods. Seleflad can be found at Edoras or the Eastfold Homesteads. You should talk to Burginda or Seleflad.\n",
[6300]="700561E5\n1\tTalk to Seleflad\tSeleflad can be found at Edoras or the Eastfold Homesteads. You should talk to Seleflad.\n",
[6301]="70000DE0\n1\tProtect Polo and fight off all the bears\tFarmer Proudfoot closed his hives to protect his bees from marauding honey-bears, but they cannot be kept closed or harm will still come to his bees. He has asked you to fend off any bears that are drawn to the honey.\n2\tTalk to Polo Proudfoot\tNow that you've driven off the bears, talk to Polo Proudfoot again for your reward.\n",
[6302]="7000B0E5\n1\tBring the honey-roasted chicken to Baldwin Foxtail\030Collect a honey-roasted chicken\tBaldwin Foxtail is at the Mathom House in Michel Delving in the Shire. Baldwin Foxtail has asked you to bring him a honey-roasted chicken for the cooks of the Mathom Society.\n",
[6303]="70067CB5\n1\tIthurga told you that the good you've done in Halrax will attract unwanted attention. He returned your tithe and told you to distribute it to the freebooters to gain favour.\t\n2\tSpeak with Ithurga at his home in Halrax\tYou distributed your tithe to the freebooters. Return to Ithurga at his home in Halrax.\n3\tTell Ithurga you will not travel to Umbar (/no)\030Tell Ithurga that you will travel to Umbar (/yes)\tIthurga asked if you will travel to Umbar. Tell him your intentions. Use the emote /yes for yes or the emote /no for no.\n4\tSpeak with Ithurga at his home in Halrax\tIthurga seems pleased with your response and wishes to speak with you one more time.\n",
[6304]="700455DF\n1\tTalk to Fastred at Kings' End\tFastred can be found at Kings' End. Burnoth has asked you to speak to Fastred about Crúmgam.\n2\tTalk to Fastred\tFastred can be found at Kings' End. Fastred has asked you to accompany him and the Riders Three into battle against Crúmgam. You should speak to him when you are prepared.\n3\tBattle on the Pelennor Fields until the day is won\tThere are many things to be done before the day is won on the Pelennor Fields. Note: You must complete Book 6, Chapter 8 of Volume IV to advance this objective.\n4\tTalk to Burnoth at Minas Tirith\030Talk to Hutha at Minas Tirith\030Talk to Ulf at Minas Tirith\tThe Riders Three can be found at the Threshold of the City. The battle is won. You should now speak to the Riders Three, and learn of what they faced after your paths diverged.\n",
})
